  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCity of Sumner City Council Vacancy (April 28, 2026) - Elections - Bremer County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n Bremer County, Iowa\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Benton County Elections\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections City of Sumner City Council Vacancy\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections by Year\n\n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2019 \n2018 \nView All\n\n\nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n\n \n \n\n \nCity of Sumner City Council Vacancy\n \nApril 28, 2026\n Special Election \n \n\n A Special Election is any election that is not regularly scheduled. A special election may be held for any purpose authorized or required by law; often to fill a vacancy or for a public measure. \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nElection Results\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n Download Official Results Results \n \n \n\n 1/1 Precincts Counted \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \nVoter Registration \n \n\n \nPre-Registration deadline for voter registration closes at 5:00pm Monday, April 13th. Persons wishing to participate in this election who register to vote after April 15 will be required to provide proof of identification (i.e. current and valid photo identification card with an expiration date), AND proof of residency in their voting precinct, when they go to the polls on election day, or when they request an absentee ballot in-person. Other provisions may also apply. Persons not registered to vote by April 15, should expect a longer processing time at the polls on election day. \n \n\nVoter ID Requirements \n \n\nClick Here for examples of acceptable voter identification requirements. \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nAbsentee Voting \n \n\n \nAbsentee Ballots will be available beginning Wednesday, May 13, for mail and in-person voting. Download the absentee ballot request form here.  \n \n \n \nThe Auditor's Office is accepting Request Forms. \n \nThe last day an absentee ballot may be mailed to a voter for this election is Monday, April 13th. \n \nIn-person absentee voting in the office of the Bremer County Auditor closes at 4:30pm on Monday, April 27. \n \nRequests for absentee ballots must be in writing and should be mailed or delivered to: Bremer County Auditor, 415 E. Bremer Ave., Waverly, Iowa 50677. \n \nMore information on Absentee Voting follow the link. \n \n \n\nAll absentee ballots must be received by 8:00pm on Election Day to be considered on time to be counted. Postmarks no longer are acceptable. \n \n\nExtended Hours \n \n\nExtended hours are available for voter registration and absentee voting in the Bremer County Auditor's Office. In addition to regular hours of Monday through Friday 8:00am to 4:30pm, extended office hours will be as follows: \n \n \n \nMonday, April 13 - 8am to 5pm \n \nThursday, April 16 - 8am to 5pm \n \nFriday, April 24 - 8am to 5pm \n \nTuesday, June 2 Election Day; Polls and Auditor's Office open from 7 a.m. to 8 p.m. \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nRunning for Office \n \n\n \nCandidate Filing Dates: \n \n \n \nFiling Deadline is Monday April 6 at 5:00pm. \n \nCandidates will need 10 signatures from City of Sumner Residents. \n \n \n\nCandidate Information Links: \n \n \n \nAffidavit of Candidacy \n \nNomination Petition \n \n \n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n \nSample Ballots \n \n\n \n\n City of Sumner City Council Vancancy\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \nBack: Past Elections\n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Bremer County, Iowa, Elections website at https://bremercountyelections.iowa.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Address\n\n 415 E. Bremer Ave.\n \nWaverly, IA 50677\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Bremer County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. \n \nPhone\n\n (319) 352-0340 \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
